@scene chapter_3_endless_bridge

background: forest_gate.png
music: mystery_forest.mp3

dialogue:
"Beyond the Gate of Choices the forest thins, and the path simply... stops."

background: valley_vista.jpg

dialogue:
"The ground falls away into a chasm so deep its bottom is only a rumour."
"On the far side, half-lost in mist, the path resumes. Between them: nothing."
"Only a weathered pillar at the cliff's lip, carved with instructions worn almost smooth."

npc You:
"There's no way across."

dialogue:
"As you speak, the air near the pillar curdles."
"A stain the colour of a healed-over wound clings to the stone — the same wrongness the System has warned of."
"The Blight. Where it touches, things forget how to work."
"Here, it has devoured the bridge itself."

system notification:
"NEW QUEST"
"THE ENDLESS BRIDGE"
"Build a path across the Blighted chasm."

dialogue:
"Far across the divide, a figure in a warden's cloak paces — three steps forward, three steps back."
"He never gets anywhere. He never stops. You call out; he does not hear."

npc System:
"The bridge was not broken, Traveller. It was UNMADE. It has forgotten how to repeat itself."
"A bridge is only one plank — laid again, and again, until it reaches the other side."

dialogue:
"The pillar's carvings flare to life."

npc System:
"To repeat an action is to LOOP. Name a count, from one up to the width of the gap."
"For each number in that count, lay a single plank. In order, none skipped, none repeated."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Loop from 1 to n. Lay each plank, in order, into the bridge."

mission: loops_intro

dialogue:
"You speak the loop. A plank of light snaps into being, then another on its echo, then a third."
"The bridge unrolls across the chasm, one plank per count, until it kisses the far edge. You cross."

background: deep_forest.jpg

dialogue:
"The pacing warden still walks his three steps, trapped in a loop that never learned to end."
"He watches you pass with hollow, envious eyes."

background: warden

npc Warden:
"You gave your loop a place to STOP, traveller. I never did. Mine has no way out."
"You counted to a number and finished. I set myself a condition that can never turn false."
"There is a difference between a loop that COUNTS and a loop that WAITS — and the second one is what ate me."
"...Remember that, when someone finally teaches you the word 'break'."

dialogue:
"He resumes his pacing. Three steps. Three steps back."
"You want to help him, and you do not yet know how."

system level_up:
"CHAPTER COMPLETE"
"The Endless Bridge"
"Applied: for loops · range · building a sequence"

reward:
xp: 100
gold: 40
achievement: BRIDGE-BUILDER

next:
chapter_3b_echoing_halls
